text:
Routes
The Routes page picks a loop (or out-and-back) from the Park Centre at the distance you choose: the same route of the day for everyone, or shuffle for another. Each comes with an elevation profile, written directions, a GPX file, an image for sharing, and palm-size cards to print for anyone running without a device (or to save as a picture on your phone). The Ultra page is one route over every trail in the park.

How routes are made and picked
The routes are made ahead of time, not on your phone. Each time the site is built, a script (07_generate_routes.py) tries about 13,500 loops from the Park Centre: out to a random trail junction A, across to another, B, and back. Each leg takes the cheapest way, where a metre of street costs 3× a metre of trail, and ground already covered costs 8× more, so legs look for new trail. Those “random” junctions come from a fixed seed, so the same data always gives the same routes. Out-and-backs go to a trail junction at half the distance and back.
Only good routes are kept: at least 80% trail, at most 10% street, and (for loops) at most 15% of the distance run twice.
Then near-copies are removed. Many good loops differ only in a short stretch, so we compare routes by the trail segments they use (a segment is the stretch between two junctions): the segments two routes share, divided by all the segments either one uses. The best routes go first (most trail, least doubling back, fewest streets), and each next route is kept only if it shares at most 75% with every route already kept. So any two routes differ in at least a quarter of their trail, about 2 km on an 8 km loop. Allowing more overlap would give more routes, but more of them would feel the same.
Route numbers are positions in that list. Loops are sorted shortest first and numbered L01, L02, … (L01 is the shortest loop); out-and-backs are OB01, OB02, …. When the data or our edits change and the site is rebuilt, the list can change, so a number isn’t a permanent name for a route.
The 7–10 km routes cover the park. Random turn points tend to miss trails close to the start and at the far north end, so after the library is built the script adds loops aimed at whatever trail no 7–10 km route runs yet, until no more good loops can be found:

coverage = FileAttachment("coverage.json").json()
md`Run as a set, the **${coverage.band_routes} routes of ${coverage.band_km[0]}–${coverage.band_km[1]} km**
(${coverage.added_for_coverage} of them added for coverage) run
**${coverage.band_trail_km} of the park's ${coverage.park_trail_km} km of trail**
(${(100 * coverage.band_trail_km / coverage.park_trail_km).toFixed(1)}%).`















Just for fun, here’s what they miss. Each bit is too short, or too awkward to reach, for a good loop, but it’s only a few metres if you want to say you’ve run the lot. “Map” opens the trail map right there.

html`&lt;table class="table table-sm"&gt;
  &lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Trail&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Length&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;
  &lt;tbody&gt;${coverage.uncovered.map((u) =&gt; html`&lt;tr&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;${u.trail}&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;${u.m} m&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;${u.dead_end ? "dead end" : ""}&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="trail_map.html#18/${u.lat}/${u.lon}" target="_blank"&gt;Map&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;/tr&gt;`)}&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;`






The Ultra page covers everything, these bits included.
The route of the day is a shuffle seeded by the date. The page keeps the routes that match your choices (type and distance), then shuffles them using today’s date in Vancouver (e.g. 2026-09-27) as the seed for its random numbers. The same seed always gives the same shuffle, so everyone who picks the same settings on the same day sees the same order:

the first route in today’s order is the route of the day, and it’s what you get when the page loads or you refresh;
Another route moves to the next one in the order, so you won’t see a repeat until you’ve been through every match;
at midnight the date changes, and so does the order;
different settings give a different list to shuffle, and so a different route.

Nothing is stored or sent anywhere: every phone does the same arithmetic. “1 of 42 matching routes” means 42 routes fit your settings, and you’re on the first in today’s order.
Sharing a route. Share opens your phone’s share sheet with the route’s name, distance, climb, written directions and a link. On a computer the button is Copy link: it copies the same text, ready to paste into an email or a message. The link ends in ?route= and a short code that fingerprints the route’s exact path, so it opens that same route (not the route of the day) for whoever you send it to. Where the phone allows, the GPX file goes along too. If the routes have been rebuilt since and that exact route is gone, the link falls back to the route of the day.

One route that runs every trail in the park at least once, starting and finishing at the Park Centre (the ranger station on Cleveland Trail at W 16th Ave). It’s also the aid station: park for free along W 16th Ave, right in the middle of the park, and there are toilets and drinking water. The route comes back past it along the way.

ultra = FileAttachment("ultra.json").json()
labels = FileAttachment("labels.geojson").json()
stats = ultra.stats

function kmRange([a, b]) {
  const [from, to] = [Math.round(a), Math.round(b)];
  return from === to ? `km ${from}` : `km ${from}–${to}`;
}

function onTheWay(kind) {
  return stats.on_the_way.filter(([, , kinds]) =&gt; kinds.includes(kind)).map(kmRange);
}
water = onTheWay("water")

html`&lt;div class="route-card"&gt;
  &lt;p class="route-stats"&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;${stats.km} km&lt;/strong&gt; ·
    &lt;strong&gt;↑ ${stats.gain_m} m ↓ ${stats.loss_m} m&lt;/strong&gt; ·
    every trail (${stats.trail_km} of ${stats.park_trail_km} km of park trail) ·
    ${stats.repeat_km} km run twice · ${stats.street_pct}% street
  &lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p class="route-stats"&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Aid station&lt;/strong&gt; (Park Centre): start,
    ${stats.aid.slice(1, -1).map(kmRange).join(", ")}, finish ·
    &lt;strong&gt;Toilets on the way&lt;/strong&gt;: ${onTheWay("toilets").join(", ")} ·
    &lt;strong&gt;Water&lt;/strong&gt;: the aid station${water.length ? `, and near ${water.join(", ")}` : " only"}
  &lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p class="route-id"&gt;Short dead-end offshoots are optional: without them it's
    ${stats.km_without_offshoots} km (they add ${stats.offshoot_km} km, out and back).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;`



















































mapDiv = html`&lt;div class="route-map ultra-map"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;`







html`&lt;div class="ultra-legend"&gt;
  &lt;span&gt;&lt;i style="background:#2a78d6"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;first time along&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span&gt;&lt;i style="background:#eb6834"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;run a second time&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span&gt;&lt;i class="dashed"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;optional offshoot&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span&gt;&lt;b class="km"&gt;5&lt;/b&gt;km marker&lt;/span&gt;
  ${Object.entries(AMENITY).map(([kind, text]) =&gt;
    html`&lt;span&gt;&lt;img src=${ICONS[kind].toDataURL()} alt=""&gt;${text.toLowerCase()}&lt;/span&gt;`)}
&lt;/div&gt;`







AMENITY = ({toilets: "Toilets", water: "Water", both: "Toilets and water"})

ICONS = {
  // The same marks as the trail map: a yellow "WC" dot, a magenta "W" dot.
  const R = 2, D = 22; // pixel ratio; one dot, in CSS px
  function dot(ctx, cx, color, letters) {
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(cx, D / 2, D / 2 - 1.5, 0, 2 * Math.PI);
    ctx.fillStyle = color;
    ctx.fill();
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.strokeStyle = "#fcfcfb";
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.fillStyle = "#0b0b0b";
    ctx.font = "700 9px system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif";
    ctx.textAlign = "center";
    ctx.textBaseline = "middle";
    ctx.fillText(letters, cx, D / 2 + 0.5);
  }
  function icon(...dots) { // dots side by side
    const width = D + (dots.length - 1) * 16;
    const canvas = Object.assign(document.createElement("canvas"), {width: width * R, height: D * R});
    canvas.style.width = `${width}px`;
    const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
    ctx.scale(R, R);
    dots.forEach(([color, letters], i) =&gt; dot(ctx, D / 2 + i * 16, color, letters));
    return canvas;
  }
  const toilets = ["#eda100", "WC"], water = ["#e87ba4", "W"];
  return {toilets: icon(toilets), water: icon(water), both: icon(toilets, water)};
}
















maplibregl = require("maplibre-gl@5.24.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js")
START = [-123.22248, 49.25918] // Park Centre
EMPTY = ({type: "FeatureCollection", features: []})

map = {
  const m = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: mapDiv,
    style: "https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron",
    center: START,
    zoom: 12.5,
    attributionControl: {customAttribution: "Trails © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL)"}
  });
  m.addControl(new maplibregl.NavigationControl(), "top-right");
  m.addControl(new maplibregl.FullscreenControl(), "top-right");
  await new Promise((resolve) =&gt; m.on("load", resolve));
  m.addSource("labels", {type: "geojson", data: labels});
  m.addSource("segments", {type: "geojson", data: ultra.segments});
  m.addSource("points", {type: "geojson", data: ultra.points});
  m.addSource("hover", {type: "geojson", data: EMPTY});
  const round = {"line-join": "round", "line-cap": "round"};
  const width = ["interpolate", ["linear"], ["zoom"], 12, 2.5, 16, 5];
  const kind = (k) =&gt; ["==", ["get", "class"], k];
  m.addLayer({id: "trails", type: "line", source: "labels", layout: round,
              filter: ["==", ["get", "kind"], "trail"],
              paint: {"line-color": "#6b8f71", "line-opacity": 0.6, "line-width": 1}});
  // Stretches run twice are drawn beside the first pass, so both show.
  m.addLayer({id: "repeat", type: "line", source: "segments", layout: round, filter: kind("repeat"),
              paint: {"line-color": "#eb6834", "line-width": width, "line-offset": 3}});
  m.addLayer({id: "first", type: "line", source: "segments", layout: round, filter: kind("first"),
              paint: {"line-color": "#2a78d6", "line-width": width}});
  m.addLayer({id: "optional", type: "line", source: "segments", filter: kind("optional"),
              paint: {"line-color": "#4a3aa7", "line-width": width, "line-dasharray": [1, 1]}});
  m.addLayer({id: "arrows", type: "symbol", source: "segments",
              layout: {"symbol-placement": "line", "symbol-spacing": 120, "text-field": "›",
                       "text-font": ["Noto Sans Bold"], "text-size": 18,
                       "text-keep-upright": false, "text-allow-overlap": true,
                       "text-ignore-placement": true},
              paint: {"text-color": "#0b0b0b"}});
  const halo = {"text-halo-color": "#fcfcfb", "text-halo-width": 1.5};
  const along = (size, font) =&gt; ({"symbol-placement": "line", "text-field": ["get", "name"],
    "text-font": [font], "text-size": size, "text-max-angle": 45, "symbol-spacing": 250});
  m.addLayer({id: "street-labels", type: "symbol", source: "labels", minzoom: 13,
              filter: ["==", ["get", "kind"], "street"], layout: along(10.5, "Noto Sans Regular"),
              paint: {"text-color": "#52514e", ...halo}});
  m.addLayer({id: "trail-labels", type: "symbol", source: "labels", minzoom: 13,
              filter: ["==", ["get", "kind"], "trail"], layout: along(11, "Noto Sans Italic"),
              paint: {"text-color": "#3d6b47", ...halo}});
  // km markers and toilets
  m.addLayer({id: "km", type: "circle", source: "points", filter: ["==", ["get", "kind"], "km"],
              paint: {"circle-radius": 11, "circle-color": "#fcfcfb",
                      "circle-stroke-color": "#0b0b0b", "circle-stroke-width": 2}});
  m.addLayer({id: "km-labels", type: "symbol", source: "points", filter: ["==", ["get", "kind"], "km"],
              layout: {"text-field": ["get", "label"], "text-font": ["Noto Sans Bold"],
                       "text-size": 11, "text-allow-overlap": true},
              paint: {"text-color": "#0b0b0b"}});
  for (const [kind, canvas] of Object.entries(ICONS)) { // the style has its own "toilets"
    const {width, height} = canvas;
    m.addImage(`amenity-${kind}`, canvas.getContext("2d").getImageData(0, 0, width, height), {pixelRatio: 2});
  }
  m.addLayer({id: "amenities", type: "symbol", source: "points",
              filter: ["in", ["get", "kind"], ["literal", Object.keys(AMENITY)]],
              layout: {"icon-image": ["concat", "amenity-", ["get", "kind"]], "icon-allow-overlap": true}});
  m.on("click", "amenities", (e) =&gt; {
    const f = e.features[0];
    new maplibregl.Popup()
      .setLngLat(f.geometry.coordinates)
      .setText(`${AMENITY[f.properties.kind]}: ${f.properties.label}`)
      .addTo(m);
  });
  m.on("mouseenter", "amenities", () =&gt; (m.getCanvas().style.cursor = "pointer"));
  m.on("mouseleave", "amenities", () =&gt; (m.getCanvas().style.cursor = ""));
  m.addLayer({id: "hover", type: "circle", source: "hover",
              paint: {"circle-radius": 7, "circle-color": "#eb6834",
                      "circle-stroke-color": "#fcfcfb", "circle-stroke-width": 2}});
  new maplibregl.Marker({color: "#0b0b0b"})
    .setLngLat(START)
    .setPopup(new maplibregl.Popup().setText("Start, finish and aid station: Park Centre (toilets and water)"))
    .addTo(m);
  const bounds = new maplibregl.LngLatBounds();
  ultra.full.forEach((c) =&gt; bounds.extend(c));
  m.fitBounds(bounds, {padding: 30, duration: 0});
  invalidation.then(() =&gt; m.remove());
  return m;
}






























profile = ultra.profile.map(([km, m, lon, lat]) =&gt; ({km, m, lon, lat}))

viewof here = {
  const low = Math.floor((d3.min(profile, (d) =&gt; d.m) - 5) / 10) * 10;
  return Plot.plot({
    width,
    height: 180,
    marginLeft: 44,
    style: {fontSize: "12px"},
    x: {label: "km →", domain: [0, stats.km]},
    y: {label: "↑ elevation (m)", domain: [low, d3.max(profile, (d) =&gt; d.m) + 5], grid: true},
    marks: [
      Plot.areaY(profile, {x: "km", y1: low, y2: "m", fill: "#2a78d6", fillOpacity: 0.12}),
      Plot.lineY(profile, {x: "km", y: "m", stroke: "#2a78d6", strokeWidth: 1.5}),
      // Aid station passes
      Plot.ruleX(stats.aid.map(([a]) =&gt; a), {stroke: "#0b0b0b", strokeDasharray: "3,3"}),
      Plot.ruleX(profile, Plot.pointerX({x: "km", stroke: "#52514e"})),
      Plot.dot(profile, Plot.pointerX({x: "km", y: "m", fill: "#eb6834", r: 4})),
      Plot.tip(profile, Plot.pointerX({x: "km", y: "m",
        title: (d) =&gt; `${d.km.toFixed(1)} km · ${Math.round(d.m)} m`}))
    ]
  });
}
















map.getSource("hover").setData(
  here?.lon
    ? {type: "Feature", geometry: {type: "Point", coordinates: [here.lon, here.lat]}}
    : EMPTY
)






Dashed lines on the profile are the passes by the aid station.

function gpx(name, coordinates) {
  const points = coordinates.map(([lon, lat]) =&gt; `&lt;trkpt lat="${lat}" lon="${lon}"&gt;&lt;/trkpt&gt;`);
  return `&lt;?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?&gt;
&lt;gpx version="1.1" creator="psp-trails" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"&gt;
  &lt;trk&gt;
    &lt;name&gt;${name}&lt;/name&gt;
    &lt;trkseg&gt;
      ${points.join("\n      ")}
    &lt;/trkseg&gt;
  &lt;/trk&gt;
&lt;/gpx&gt;`;
}

html`&lt;div class="route-actions"&gt;
  ${DOM.download(
    () =&gt; new Blob([gpx(`Pacific Spirit every trail (${stats.km} km)`, ultra.full)],
                   {type: "application/gpx+xml"}),
    "psp-every-trail.gpx",
    "Download GPX"
  )}
  ${DOM.download(
    () =&gt; new Blob([gpx(`Pacific Spirit every trail, no offshoots (${stats.km_without_offshoots} km)`, ultra.main)],
                   {type: "application/gpx+xml"}),
    "psp-every-trail-no-offshoots.gpx",
    "GPX without offshoots"
  )}
&lt;/div&gt;`
















Directions

html`&lt;details class="cue-details"&gt;&lt;summary&gt;All ${ultra.directions.length} turns&lt;/summary&gt;
  &lt;ol class="directions"&gt;${ultra.directions.map(([km, full]) =&gt;
    html`&lt;li class=${full.startsWith("Optional") ? "optional" : ""}&gt;&lt;span class="at-km"&gt;${km.toFixed(1)}&lt;/span&gt; ${full}&lt;/li&gt;`
  )}&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;`








Where this idea comes from
Running every trail in Pacific Spirit as one ultra isn’t our idea: there’s an existing Pacific Spirit Park ultra route that inspired this page. We’ll link it, and its GPX, here. What’s on this page is our own version, worked out from the trail data by code.


How it’s made
Finding the shortest run that covers every trail is a classic puzzle, the route inspection or “Chinese postman” problem. Every junction needs as many ways in as ways out; where a junction doesn’t have that (a dead end, or three trails meeting), some stretch has to be run twice, or linked up by road. It’s an ultra already, so a bit of road beats running a trail a second time: the script (08_plan_ultra.py) counts a repeat as 2½ times the distance and road as 1½ times (Imperial Drive and W 29th Ave, which we run anyway, count the same as trail), picks the cheapest way to join everything up, and walks it all as one loop from the Park Centre. It only turns straight back at a dead end; dead-end offshoots of up to 400 m are marked optional. It uses the same trail data and edits as the Routes page; see About.

Pick a distance and a route type. Everyone who opens this page on the same day, with the same choices, gets the same route of the day; Another route shuffles. Routes stay on park trails as much as possible and use streets only to link trails up.

function rangeSlider({min, max, step, value, label}) {
  const form = html`&lt;form class="range2"&gt;
    &lt;label&gt;${label}&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;div class="range2-track"&gt;
      &lt;input type="range" name="lo" min=${min} max=${max} step=${step} value=${value[0]} aria-label="Shortest"&gt;
      &lt;input type="range" name="hi" min=${min} max=${max} step=${step} value=${value[1]} aria-label="Longest"&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;output name="out"&gt;&lt;/output&gt;
  &lt;/form&gt;`;
  const {lo, hi, out} = form.elements;
  const track = form.querySelector(".range2-track");
  const pct = (v) =&gt; `${(100 * (v - min)) / (max - min)}%`;
  const update = () =&gt; {
    form.value = [+lo.value, +hi.value];
    out.value = `${lo.value}–${hi.value} km`;
    track.style.setProperty("--lo", pct(lo.value));
    track.style.setProperty("--hi", pct(hi.value));
  };
  form.addEventListener("input", (event) =&gt; {
    // Thumbs can't pass each other.
    if (+lo.value &gt; +hi.value) {
      if (event.target === lo) lo.value = hi.value;
      else hi.value = lo.value;
    }
    update();
  });
  form.addEventListener("submit", (event) =&gt; event.preventDefault());
  update();
  return form;
}

DEFAULT_TYPES = ["Loop"]
DEFAULT_KM = [7, 10]

viewof types = Inputs.checkbox(["Loop", "Out-and-back"], {
  label: "Route type",
  value: DEFAULT_TYPES
})
viewof km = rangeSlider({min: 4, max: 12, step: 0.5, value: DEFAULT_KM, label: "Distance"})
viewof again = Inputs.button("Another route")












































routes = FileAttachment("routes.geojson").json()

matching = routes.features.filter(
  (f) =&gt;
    types.map((t) =&gt; t.toLowerCase()).includes(f.properties.type) &&
    f.properties.km &gt;= km[0] &&
    f.properties.km &lt;= km[1]
)

// Today in Vancouver, as YYYY-MM-DD: the seed for the route of the day.
today = new Date().toLocaleDateString("en-CA", {timeZone: "America/Vancouver"})

// FNV-1a string hash: turns the date into a number, the same on every phone.
function hash(text) {
  let h = 2166136261;
  for (const c of text) h = Math.imul(h ^ c.charCodeAt(0), 16777619);
  return h &gt;&gt;&gt; 0;
}

// mulberry32: random numbers from a seed. Same seed, same sequence, anywhere.
function seeded(seed) {
  return () =&gt; {
    seed = (seed + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;
    let t = Math.imul(seed ^ (seed &gt;&gt;&gt; 15), 1 | seed);
    t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t &gt;&gt;&gt; 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;
    return ((t ^ (t &gt;&gt;&gt; 14)) &gt;&gt;&gt; 0) / 4294967296;
  };
}

// Today's order for the matching routes: a Fisher-Yates shuffle seeded by the
// date. Everyone gets the same order; "Another route" steps along it, so no
// route repeats until you've seen them all.
order = {
  const random = seeded(hash(today));
  const idx = matching.map((_, i) =&gt; i);
  for (let i = idx.length - 1; i &gt; 0; i--) {
    const j = Math.floor(random() * (i + 1));
    [idx[i], idx[j]] = [idx[j], idx[i]];
  }
  return idx;
}

// A shared link (…/routes.html?route=&lt;key&gt;) shows that route until you
// change a setting or ask for another.
sharedKey = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get("route")
sharedRoute = routes.features.find((f) =&gt; f.properties.key === sharedKey) ?? null
useShared =
  sharedRoute !== null &&
  again === 0 &&
  types.join() === DEFAULT_TYPES.join() &&
  km.join() === DEFAULT_KM.join()

position = matching.length ? again % matching.length : 0

route = useShared
  ? sharedRoute
  : matching.length
    ? matching[order[position]]
    : null















































































route
  ? html`&lt;div class="route-card"&gt;
      &lt;h3&gt;${route.properties.name}&lt;/h3&gt;
      &lt;p class="route-stats"&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;${route.properties.km.toFixed(1)} km&lt;/strong&gt; ${route.properties.type} ·
        &lt;strong&gt;↑ ${route.properties.gain_m} m ↓ ${route.properties.loss_m} m&lt;/strong&gt; ·
        ${route.properties.trail_pct}% trail · ${route.properties.street_pct}% street
        &lt;span class="route-id"&gt;· route ${route.properties.id} ·
        ${useShared
          ? "shared with you"
          : `${again === 0 ? "route of the day" : "another route"}: ${position + 1} of ${matching.length} matching routes`}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/p&gt;
      ${sharedKey && !sharedRoute
        ? html`&lt;p class="route-note"&gt;The shared route isn't in the current list
            (routes are rebuilt when the trail data changes), so here's today's route.&lt;/p&gt;`
        : ""}
    &lt;/div&gt;`
  : html`&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;No routes match. Widen the distance or tick another route type.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;`







mapDiv = html`&lt;div class="route-map"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;`







maplibregl = require("maplibre-gl@5.24.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js")

START = [-123.22248, 49.25918] // Park Centre
// Named trails and streets (step 05): context lines and labels.
labels = FileAttachment("labels.geojson").json()
EMPTY = ({type: "FeatureCollection", features: []})

map = {
  const m = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: mapDiv,
    style: "https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron",
    center: START,
    zoom: 13.5,
    attributionControl: {
      customAttribution: "Trails © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL)"
    }
